    <div id="storyPopup" class="popup">

        <div class="popup-box">

            <label for="story" class="close">&times;</label>

            <h2 class="popup-title">🦸 Courage Over Fear</h2>

            <div class="composition">


                <div class="composition-text">

                    <h3>Exposition</h3>

                    <p>
                        Biboy started saying, “Do you think I’m messing around?” Biboy then pulled out a two-pronged fork. Baljeit was shocked. Baljeit cried out, “Please don’t hurt me!”
                    </p>


                    <h3>Inciting Incident</h3>

                    <p>
                        In the city of Farmtropolis, a sheep named Baljeit Da Sheep lived. Baljeit wasn’t like any other sheep; he was intelligent. He only had one friend, Dinkity Da Horsity. Baljeit was on his way to his new school, named Chikren University for Gifted Animals. On the way, he picked up Dinkity from his house, and they started their journey to school. As they entered the school, a pig came up to them and said, “Yo, what are these poor, broke, needy, charity, platelicker animals doing here? Get out of my campus right now, peasants!” As Baljeit tried to stand up for themselves, the pig shoved past them and exclaimed in disgust. A little duck came up to them and said, “What are you guys doing? Are you guys trying to get killed?” Baljeit replied, “I’m sorry, but who was he?” The duck responded, “He’s Biboy Biggy Ur-Nammu, the son of the university’s principal’s best friend! He can get you guys expelled from this school!” After learning this, Baljeit and Dinkity started avoiding Biboy and his gang, but it wasn’t until they found out they were in the same class as him and his friends. As days turned into weeks, Dinkity became the laughingstock of the class because of his appearance, while Baljeit simply flew under the radar to avoid the bullying. Dinkity felt betrayed and avoided Baljeit.
                    </p>


                    <h3>Rising Action</h3>

                    <p>
                        One day, Baljeit finally stood up for Dinkity, resulting in Biboy throwing a tantrum at Baljeit. Biboy shouted in anger, “HOW DARE YOU USELESS LITTLE LOW-LIFE TALK BACK TO ME!” As Baljeit realized what he had done, he ran out of the classroom and into the nearby restroom. He was startled by the janitor cleaning the restroom. The janitor asked why he was in such a panic; Baljeit then replied, stuttering, “I accidentally angered Biboy; please don’t tell him I’m here.” The janitor responded, “I won’t; don’t worry.” Baljeit thanked the janitor and asked what his name was. The janitor then said, “My name is Johnni Torres. I’ve been working for this university since the first day of its opening.” Baljeit was finally feeling relieved until he heard footsteps right outside the door. Biboy barged into the restroom and stumbled upon Johnni Torres all alone, with no sign of Baljeit. Biboy clicked his tongue and said, “Oi, have you seen a sheep running around here?” The unbothered bull just shook his head and continued to mop the restroom floors. Biboy stomped his feet and fled the restroom. Baljeit asked, “Is he gone?” Johnni replied, “Yeah, kid, he’s gone.” As Baljeit emerged from the cubicle, he thanked Johnni and went out of the restroom to head into his next class; thankfully, Biboy wasn’t in that class. As the school day went by, Biboy and his gang were waiting for Baljeit at the university’s gates. Then, Baljeit slipped into the crowd, running for dear life. As Baljeit navigated through the busy crowd of Chikren University, he noticed Biboy’s gang waiting at every exit of the campus. He didn’t have a choice but to run back to the kind and wise janitor, Johnni Torres. After a few close calls from Biboy’s Gang, the trembling sheep finally made his way to Johnni’s usual area. Johnni, the calm, collected bull, asked, “What's with the rush, Kid?” Baljeit took one last peek outside the utility room door and finally replied to Johnni, “They’re still on my tail, Mr. Johnni.” Johnni chuckled and exclaimed, “Mr. Johnni...” and exclaimed, “Am I that old, Kid? Johnni is okay.” Baljeit started stuttering, and Johnni chuckled and blurted out, “Jeez, you're a timid one.” After a few minutes of silence, Baljeit finally picked up the courage to peek out the door again and, to no surprise, the hall was still crowded; but there were no signs of Biboy’s Gang anywhere. Baljeit turned to Johnni and bowed down deeply and said, “Thank you, Johnni. I won’t forget about you.” Johnni acknowledged his kind and genuine words and gave him a pat on the back. “Don’t mention it. Be careful out there.” Baljeit smiled warmly and closed the door behind him as he left. As he walked through the busy and loud crowd, as he walked closer to the exit, every step he took felt like he was being watched, and sure enough, the furious and fuming pig alongside his gang ran after Baljeit, making the timid little sheep run blindly. After minutes of running, he finally got cornered by Biboy and his gang in an alleyway. Baljeit, with no other choice, backed up into the corner of the alley.
                    </p>


                    <h3>Climax</h3>

                    <p>
                        Biboy and his gang surrounded the trembling little sheep, and Baljeit thought to himself, “Oh jeez, what am I supposed to do?” He eventually backed up to the cold brick wall of the alley, then wondered to himself, “Why am I even putting up with this? I’m sick and tired of this nepo baby!” Before he could speak up, Biboy started saying, “Do you think I’m messing around?” Biboy then pulled out a two-pronged fork. Baljeit was shocked and started backing up more, despite the brick wall behind the frail and trembling sheep. Before Biboy could stab Baljeit, a big, smelly cow shoved the raging pig, enraging Biboy more. Biboy snapped back at the cow, “WHO IN THE LAMB CHOPS ARE YOU?” The cow then scoffed at the fuming pig and retorted, “It’s none of your business.” Then he reached into his pockets, making Biboy and his gang tremble, and his gang left him there all alone. The once-raging pig was now trembling. The cow stomped his foot, and Biboy went running, while Baljeit stood there, frozen and curious about who this cow was. The cow, noticing the tension in Baljeit, said, “Relax, I won’t hurt you.” The curious sheep tilted his head at the cow, still confused. The cow chuckled and said, “My name is Moocus Moo III, but you can call me Moo.” Baljeit nodded in respect and bowed down. After a few seconds, he quickly added, “Thanks, Moo. He finally got what he deserved.”
                    </p>


                    <h3>Falling Action</h3>

                    <p>
                        After the tense altercation with Biboy, Baljeit roamed the streets of Farmtropolis with the sun already setting. For a few moments, it was finally peaceful for Baljeit. As it became darker, he finally arrived back at his old shack. He entered and quickly fixed his boots near the door and walked to his futon to get some rest. As the tired sheep lay there, he thought to himself, “I hope Dinkity is alright,” and went to bed. The next morning, he was woken up by his friend knocking on the door, Dinkity Da Horsity. This only meant one thing. Baljeit was late for school. Without wasting any time, Baljeit didn't bother to take a shower; he ran to his boots, nearly tripping, but successfully grabbed the boots and opened the door. As the doorknob twisted, Baljeit immediately knelt down to fix his boots. After a few moments, Baljeit finally finished fixing his boots. The Horse and the Sheep ran through the slums of Farmtropolis, just a normal day for the two. As they ran, they saw a limousine with two arguing pigs inside: Biboy Biggy Ur-nammu and his father, Bong Biggie Namu, the mayor. Curiosity got the best of Baljeit and Dinkity, and they walked closer to the limousine, crouching behind the window. As they remained there, they were overhearing the conversation of the Mayor of Farmtropolis and the “Notorious Bully of Chikren University”. Biboy fumed in response, “Father, It’s not my fault that I woke up late!” and then Bong snapped back with, “I told you many times to sleep early! What did you do? You slept late, yet again!” Biboy retaliated verbally, “I SLEPT AROUND 10-11 PM! HOW IS THAT CONSIDERED LATE?” Then, Bong looked at his son in disgust, then slapped him, leaving a handmark on Biboy’s cheek and snapped at his son, “HOW DARE YOU TALK TO UR FATHER LIKE THAT! I DID NOT RAISE YOU TO BE DISRESPECTFUL!” After receiving those words, Biboy just sat there stunned and tearing up while holding his red cheek. And for a few moments, the parked limousine that was once loud grew quiet. Biboy kicked the conventional doors open and slammed them behind him, running to his empire inside the campus of Chikren University. Baljeit and Dinkity finally stood up from their position, shocked not just by the argument, but by the Mayor’s actions towards his own son.

                        <br><br>

                        <i>FLASHBACK</i><br><br>

                        Biboy wasn't always like this; he used to be kind and charitable to others. Due to his father's abuse and neglect, Biboy grew up with bad habits like being arrogant, thinking everything can be solved with money, and so on. His father, the Mayor, was always busy, causing him to neglect his one and only son.

                        <br><br>

                        <i>PRESENT</i><br><br>

                        Baljeit and Dinkity snapped out of their trance and ran after Biboy, hoping to cheer him up.
                    </p>


                    <h3>Resolution</h3>

                    <p>
                        Baljeit and Dinkity caught up to Biboy; he sat in the desolate gym closet, crying and sniffling. When Biboy saw Baljeit and Dinkity, Biboy quickly wiped his tears and snapped at the two, “What are you two losers doing here?” He tried masking this moment of vulnerability with anger, but it clearly didn't work. Baljeit and Dinkity closed the sliding door, entered the desolate closet, and walked up to Biboy, giving the poor vulnerable pig a warm hug. Biboy tried resisting, but melted into the hug. He cried onto Baljeit and Dinkity’s shoulders, crying like never before. After a few moments of comforting the bawling pig, he felt something he never ever felt before, he felt safe and secured. Baljeit broke the silence first, “We saw what your father did. I’m so sorry, Biboy.” and Dinkity quickly added “We’re here for you, friend.”. Biboy smiled at them and hugged tighter. After a few more years, it was finally time to graduate. At the Farmtropolis Auditorium, Baljeit, Dinkity, and Biboy take their final photo with Johnni and Moocus. Baljeit grew up and fell in love with Rose Ann, a nice and kind pig; together, they had a family of 4. Dinkity on the other hand remained single but became a lawyer dedicated to fighting for Transgender Rights. Lastly, Biboy followed in his father’s footsteps despite their history.
                    </p>

                </div>


                <div class="composition-picture">

                    <img src="shortstory.jpg.jpg"
                         alt="Courage Over Fear">

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>

    </div>



